      "summary": "The article argues that Freeport-McMoRan is a safer investment than MP Materials for those betting on a metals supercycle driven by electrification and AI infrastructure. While both companies benefit from rising copper and rare earth demand, Freeport-McMoRan presents lower execution risk with established production recovery plans and cost-effective expansion initiatives, whereas MP Materials faces execution risks from its Texas magnet facility construction and Chinese export controls on rare-earth processing technology.",
